bad_rcpt_to.cmy triggers a real SPF lookup for the MAIL FROM domain.
testy.com is now a parked domain publishing "v=spf1 -all", so chasquid
correctly rejects the MAIL FROM and the test fails. Use the RFC 2606
reserved .invalid TLD instead, which can never have an SPF record.

--- a/test/t-12-minor_dialogs/bad_rcpt_to.cmy
+++ b/test/t-12-minor_dialogs/bad_rcpt_to.cmy
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 c <~ 220
 c -> HELO localhost
 c <~ 250
-c -> MAIL FROM:<test@testy.com>
+c -> MAIL FROM:<test@testy.invalid>
 c <~ 250
 
 c -> RCPT LALA: <>
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 c <~ 220
 c -> HELO localhost
 c <~ 250
-c -> MAIL FROM:<test@testy.com>
+c -> MAIL FROM:<test@testy.invalid>
 c <~ 250
 
 c -> RCPT TO:<pepe>
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
 c <~ 220
 c -> HELO localhost
 c <~ 250
-c -> MAIL FROM:<test@testy.com>
+c -> MAIL FROM:<test@testy.invalid>
 c <~ 250
 
 c -> RCPT TO:<a@b/c>
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 c <~ 220
 c -> HELO localhost
 c <~ 250
-c -> MAIL FROM:<test@testy.com>
+c -> MAIL FROM:<test@testy.invalid>
 c <~ 250
 
 c -> RCPT TO:<henryⅣ@testserver>
